## 2. State Machine & Logic Flow

The system operates in a state machine governed by the sampling timer. The logical flow ensures that transient noise does not trigger alerts.

```text
[START]
   |
   +--> INIT (Hardware setup, Zero counters)
   |
   +--> [WAIT_FOR_SAMPLE]
   |     |
   |     +--(Time >= Interval) --> [READ_SENSOR]
   |     |                          |
   |     |                          +--(Read OK?)
   |     |                          |   Yes --> [FILTER_DATA]
   |     |                          |   No  --> [MARK_ERROR]
   |     |
   |     +--(Time < Interval) --> [WAIT_FOR_SAMPLE]
   |
   +--> [FILTER_DATA]
   |     (Calculate Moving Avg of last 3 samples)
   |
   +--> [EVALUATE_STATUS]
   |     (Compare Avg Temp vs Thresholds)
   |     |
   |     +--> Normal (10-40°C) --> Reset Fault Counters
   |     |
   |     +--> Warning (0-10 or 40-60°C) --> Increment Warning Count
   |     |
   |     +--> Fault (<0 or >60°C) --> Increment Fault Counter
   |
   +--> [REPORT_IF_CHANGE]
   |     (If Status changed since last report)
   |
   +--> [WAIT_FOR_SAMPLE] (Loop)
```

